# Opt-in switch for local embeddings: copy to
# ~/.config/goblin-memory/embed-relay.env and install.py picks up the
# goblin-embed-* units — a socat relay that lets the bridge-net API
# container reach the host ollama, plus a keep-alive pin timer.
# ADDR must be a host-local IPv4, never a LAN one: ollama 403s non-local
# Host headers and only loopback sources should reach this relay at all
# (the unit's range= admits only this /32). The tailscale address works —
# stable, host-local, not on the LAN; tailnet peers can reach the port,
# and range= rejects them.
GOBLIN_EMBED_RELAY_ADDR=
GOBLIN_EMBED_MODEL=embeddinggemma
